WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:04.120
What's next for the web-head as he heads back
into action and looks for things to return

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:06.740
to normal in his second MCU solo film?

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:10.900
We've got all the answers you're looking for
with this look at everything you need to know

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:13.280
before watching Spider-Man: Far from Home.

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:18.340
One of the most compelling things about Spider-Man:
Far from Home will be how Marvel chooses to

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:22.860
handle their first film after the incredibly
disruptive events of Avengers: Endgame.

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:27.900
Far From Home will definitely be more modest
in scale compared the cosmic events of Endgame,

00:00:27.910 --> 00:00:33.340
Infinity War and Captain Marvel, Peter's going
to Europe, not space, but it can't ignore

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:36.000
the effects of the last two Avengers films.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.860
Far from Home will be the first time Marvel
really shows us what the MCU looks like after

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:42.240
the Infinity Saga.

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:46.800
One of the biggest effects that Endgame had
on the MCU was a sudden jump five years into

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:47.700
the future.

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:52.320
Endgame co-directors Anthony and Joe Russo
have confirmed that the time jump means those

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:56.420
who were saved from Thanos' initial snap ended
up five years younger than everyone that had

00:00:56.420 --> 00:00:57.420
survived.

00:00:57.520 --> 00:01:02.200
It appears from the Spider-Man: Far from Home
trailers that many of Peter Parker's closest

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:05.930
friends and classmates still seem to still
be around the same age, which indicates that

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:08.300
they were probably all dusted together.

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:13.200
Best pals Ned and Peter, and apparently Mary
Jane were all snapped, and will consequently

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:16.000
still be the same age going into Far from
Home.

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:20.780
Perhaps the biggest can of worms that Endgame
opened up was the concept of time travel,

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:23.040
which inevitably leads to the multiverse.

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:27.020
It was already difficult to contain the effects
of time travel and the various branch realities

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:29.820
it creates within the plot of Endgame on its
own.

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:34.420
The alterations it can create could begin
to make MCU continuity start to feel a little

00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:35.840
bit like herding cats.

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:38.460
Marvel's steering right into the skid, though.

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:40.660
"We could have used someone like you on my world."

00:01:40.660 --> 00:01:41.300
"Your world?"

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:43.360
"Beck is from Earth. Just not ours."

00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:48.560
The hard left into the multiverse concept
is impressive, but the question is, will it

00:01:48.569 --> 00:01:53.069
hold up this many years into a universe that
has barely sniffed at any of these concepts

00:01:53.069 --> 00:01:54.180
up until now?

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:57.960
And is Mysterio even telling the truth about
where he's from?

00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:02.940
Historically, Quentin Beck has been a master
of illusion and misdirection, and Mysterio

00:02:02.950 --> 00:02:07.430
is well-known as one of Spider-Man's classic
antagonists, even though the trailers are

00:02:07.430 --> 00:02:09.520
clearly spinning him as more of a hero.

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:13.840
Common sense would dictate that the promotional
footage is simply warming up a character that

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:18.680
loves to fool others, and that he will ultimately
be revealed as a villain.

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:23.340
Marvel and Disney have become quite good at
promotional misdirects themselves, with multiple

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:26.640
trailers that have misled or outright lied
to fans.

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:31.439
When you consider that Marvel also basically
rewrote the entire script on the Skrulls in

00:02:31.439 --> 00:02:36.450
Captain Marvel, flipping them from evil aliens
to sympathetic refugees, it makes the entire

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:38.920
Mysterio situation a bit of an enigma.

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:43.719
It's worth noting that the notion that Mysterio
has heroic aspirations is also seemingly a

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:45.200
sort of in-joke.

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:50.400
Jake Gyllenhaal, who plays Beck, came tantalizingly
close to taking over the role of Spider-Man

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:54.280
after Tobey Maguire sustained a back injury
between the first and second Sam Raimi-directed

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:55.280
films.

00:02:55.400 --> 00:03:00.820
Mysterio crosses paths with Peter Parker because
of the looming threat of the Elementals, A

00:03:00.830 --> 00:03:03.709
trio of destructive beings wreaking havoc.

00:03:03.709 --> 00:03:06.860
They appear to be composed of water, fire
and earth.

00:03:06.860 --> 00:03:11.400
According to a ScreenRant set report, Far
from Home will reveal the origins of these

00:03:11.410 --> 00:03:15.730
additions to Spidey's rogues' gallery, and
there's also evidence to suggest that they're

00:03:15.730 --> 00:03:20.880
tied in some way to the classic comics villains
Sandman, Molten Man, and Hydro-Man.

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:25.100
It's easy to assume that Mysterio is really
behind the whole thing, but however the story

00:03:25.110 --> 00:03:29.280
ends up breaking down, Spider-Man will have
his webs full when it comes to bad guys this

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:30.280
time around.

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:35.580
There will never be another Tony Stark, but
it looks like the MCU is angling to have Spider-Man

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:38.520
fill an important need following Stark's death
in Endgame.

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:40.920
"I just really miss him."

00:03:41.380 --> 00:03:43.680
"Yeah, I miss him, too."

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:49.200
Parker has typically been portrayed as a young
man both in print and onscreen, and the idea

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:52.920
of him looking up to a mentor or wanting to
impress other superheroes is hardly a new

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:53.920
concept.

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:59.099
In the MCU in particular, Iron Man has always
been the hero that has stood tallest in Parker's

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:01.960
eyes, beginning all the way back in Iron Man
2.

00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:04.959
Parker is unlikely to ever become Iron Man...

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:07.280
"I'd rather just stay on the ground for a
little while.

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:09.480
Friendly neighborhood Spider-Man."

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:14.820
but it seems likely that he'll be called on
to step into the gap left by Stark's death.

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:19.100
The move would be a natural one, considering
their history, and would make for good storytelling

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:23.421
as Parker processes his loss and is faced
with some of the less savory elements of the

00:04:23.421 --> 00:04:24.420
superhero life.

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:28.420
Far from Home promises to introduce several
new Spidey suits.

00:04:28.420 --> 00:04:32.320
While we already know from the trailers that
we'll get to see the Iron Spider armor from

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:36.790
the Avengers films, there have also been hints
of upgrades to the more classic look, as well

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:42.290
as an entirely black stealth suit, a S.H.I.E.L.D.-inspired
outfit that takes quite a bit of inspiration

00:04:42.290 --> 00:04:45.700
from the uniforms of past agents, including
Black Widow and Hawkeye.

00:04:45.700 --> 00:04:50.140
Executive producer Eric Carroll explained
that, while the suit was originally pretty

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:52.710
high-tech, they ended up dumbing it down quite
a bit.

00:04:52.710 --> 00:04:56.970
It was too high-powered, so the filmmakers
ended up making it, quote, "less cool" to

00:04:56.970 --> 00:04:58.420
better fit Parker's character.

00:04:58.420 --> 00:05:03.980
When you see him flipping up those goggles
by hand, know that it's absolutely on purpose.

00:05:03.980 --> 00:05:06.000
Tom Holland's favorite thing about the suit?

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:09.880
It makes it a lot easier for the poor guy
to use the bathroom between takes.

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:14.800
Sony, not Marvel Studios, owns the rights
to Spider-Man, along with quite a few related

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:15.800
characters.

00:05:15.820 --> 00:05:20.560
There was a harrowing moment in 1999 when
Marvel actually offered nearly all of its

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:23.060
existing characters to Sony for a paltry sum.

00:05:23.060 --> 00:05:27.560
While Sony only nabbed the rights to Spidey
and friends, the webhead was still sorely

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:29.620
missed when the MCU took off in earnest.

00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:31.180
"Underoos!"

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:42.240
In 2015, Sony and Marvel struck a unique shared-custody
deal that allowed Peter Parker to show up

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:45.780
in multiple MCU films while remaining a property
of Sony.

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:49.560
A lot about that deal remains unknown to the
public, with Vanity Fair having referred to

00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:52.460
the arrangement as being, quote “densely
complicated.”

00:05:52.460 --> 00:05:56.880
Some outlets have reported that the deal could
be up after Far from Home, which might leave

00:05:56.880 --> 00:05:59.960
an interesting question mark at the end of
Parker's adventures abroad.

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:03.600
Will this be the last we see of the crime-fighting
spider in the MCU?

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:05.380
Is the current deal still going?

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:09.580
Or will Sony and Marvel hammer out a new agreement,
keeping the shared custody arrangement going

00:06:09.580 --> 00:06:10.580
indefinitely?

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:14.520
The question is a big one, as it'll determine
whether Spidey will be an important part of

00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:19.660
the MCU in the years to come, or if Far From
Home will be Tom Holland Spidey's swan song.

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:25.280
Spider-Man: Far from Home is the official
endcap for Phase 3 of the MCU, and it'll also

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:28.700
be the last time a Marvel movie is released
for nearly a year.

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:33.740
Far from Home swings into theaters on July
2, 2019, and the next Marvel movie won't be

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:36.160
released until May 1, 2020.

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:41.780
That's 304 days without a new Marvel movie,
the longest gap in quite some time.

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:43.700
"Parker, you're late, man!

00:06:43.700 --> 00:06:44.840
Always late!"

00:06:45.080 --> 00:06:50.120
The good news is, once the dust of Phase 3
finally settles, we're likely to get quite

00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:51.900
a bit more info on what's coming.

00:06:51.940 --> 00:06:55.970
The soon-to-launch Disney+ streaming service
will likely help fill in some of the gaps.

00:06:55.970 --> 00:07:00.250
Fans who plan on subscribing should be able
to get a bit of a fix in some way or another,

00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:04.630
whether that's through watching past Marvel
movies or indulging in the various MCU-related

00:07:04.630 --> 00:07:07.300
limited series that Marvel is producing for
the platform.

00:07:07.300 --> 00:07:13.140
But Far from Home is our last chance to enjoy
the MCU on the big screen for nearly a year,

00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:14.720
so take advantage while you can.

00:07:14.880 --> 00:07:17.020
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:07:17.020 --> 00:07:20.420
Plus, even more Looper videos about Spider-Man
are coming soon.

00:07:20.420 --> 00:07:24.840
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

